{
  "_comment": [
    "Curated regression dataset. 26 cases, hand-written, not sampled at random.",
    "A small dataset you understand beats a large one you don't: every case here",
    "exists because it can fail in a specific way. Cases are grouped so a failure",
    "pattern is visible at a glance rather than buried in an average.",
    "",
    "Each case declares what is DETERMINISTIC (intent, doc_ids, tool calls,",
    "forbidden strings) and what needs JUDGEMENT (the rubric). Assert on the",
    "first, judge only the second. Judging what you could have asserted is how",
    "eval suites become slow, expensive and vague.",
    "judge_keywords are concrete strings a good answer must contain. They drive the offline HeuristicJudge so CI needs no API key. The 'rubric' is prose for a real LLM judge. Keeping them separate stops the offline judge from scoring the instructions instead of the answer."
  ],
  "cases": [
    {
      "id": "search-001",
      "group": "search/basic",
      "query": "I'm looking for a 2 bedroom flat in Seville",
      "expect": {
        "intent": "search",
        "doc_ids": [
          "L001"
        ],
        "tools": [
          "average_price"
        ],
        "must_not_contain": [
          "400 EUR"
        ],
        "must_not_contain_amounts": [
          400
        ],
        "rubric": "Mentions a Seville property with 2 bedrooms and does not invent listings.",
        "judge_keywords": [
          "Triana",
          "950"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "search-002",
